35,2,1,talk,Ryuji,,"A full pass takes over an hour and a half. Also, outside firms require us to tidy up before they even arrive.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Mio,,"It's a mess! Some of us are barely here, while a few people do almost all the cooking and cleaning.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Victoria,,Our chat history is full of reminders that lead to fights. The previous tenants tried permanent roles and stopped speaking.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Rin,,"We're wasting money buying the same spray twice! And the management office charges 4,200 yen an hour!","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Daisuke,,"We all have different ideas of ""clean."" Also, the bathroom grout gets dirty again in just eleven days.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Ryuji,,"@Victoria, if permanent roles led to silence, we must avoid that. But the time commitment is significant regardless of the system.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Mio,,"@Ryuji, exactly. If only a few people use the kitchen, it's unfair for everyone to share the work equally.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Victoria,,"@Mio, that's the danger. If we focus only on ""fair"" usage, we might end up in the same conflict as the previous tenants.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Rin,,"@Rin, wait, I'm talking to myself! @Victoria, if we pay a pro, does that stop the fighting? It's expensive, but maybe worth it!","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Daisuke,,"@Daisuke, I mean... @Rin, if the bathroom gets dirty so fast, maybe a rota isn't enough. It's just... stressful.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Ryuji,,"@Daisuke, the physical constraints of the bathroom mean more frequent work. We need a system that doesn't feel like a burden.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Mio,,"@Ryuji, but a rota ignores that some people are away for whole months. We can't have a fixed schedule for that.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Victoria,,"@Mio, a flexible system is good, but ambiguity is where the rows start. We need clear expectations.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Rin,,But the money is a problem! We aren't settling up for the supplies. We need a way to track the costs!,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Daisuke,,"I just don't want to walk into a grim kitchen. If we can't agree on ""done,"" we'll always be unhappy.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
