60,3,1,talk,Ryuji,,Option A is risky based on Victoria's findings. Option B is a burden. Option C is expensive but removes the labor.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Mio,,Option B is unfair to those who are away. Option A is too rigid. Option C seems the most balanced for our habits.,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Victoria,,"Option A is a disaster waiting to happen. Option B leads to the ""reminders"" that cause rows. Option C is the safest for our friendship.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Rin,,"Option C is pricey, but it solves the ""who does what"" and ""who pays"" if we just split the bill!","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Daisuke,,I like Option C. I wouldn't have to worry about whether the person before me actually cleaned the bathroom.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Ryuji,,"@Rin, the cost is high, but the time saved is higher. It removes the administrative burden of a rota.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Mio,,"@Ryuji, I agree. It's better to pay a bit more than to feel resentful about who's using the kitchen.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Victoria,,"@Mio, exactly. The social cost of a failed rota is far higher than the monthly fee for a service.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Rin,,I'm voting for C! Let's just make a group pot for the supplies and the cleaner!,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Daisuke,,I agree with Rin. Option C is the only one that makes me feel relaxed about the house.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Ryuji,,I'll vote for C. It's the most rational way to ensure the work is actually done to a professional standard.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Mio,,I'm with you all. Option C is the most fair given our different schedules and usage levels.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Victoria,,I vote for C. Preserving our relationship is more important than saving a few thousand yen.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Rin,,Yay! Everyone likes the pro cleaner! I'm so excited for a sparkly house!,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Daisuke,,I'm voting for C too. It's the best choice for my peace of mind.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
